/-!
# Reduced analytic frontier of `HESSIAN-GLOBAL-01`

The primitive SpinC packet is closed by the implemented geometry: the Clifford
signs, connection compatibility, invariant-flow decomposition, intrinsic-frame
integration by parts and global Green current construct the exact maximal
same-action matter graph for every mass.

The three remaining analytic packets now have constructive normal forms:

* the local family asks for `C²` only on the seven physical action blocks;
  matter and LL regularity are derived from their smooth quadratic graph
  actions;
* the H11 common bound is the finite sum of seven named block estimates;
* the H12 defects are canonical (`I - QH` and `I - HQ`) and are generated by
  one generalized inverse satisfying `HQH = H`.

Thus the irreducible obligations are exposed at their natural analytic level:
seven local physical regularity statements, seven blockwise estimates, and one
bounded generalized inverse with finite canonical defect ranges. The imported
constructive closure composes these directly into the H14 certificate without a
D10 direction or replacement action.
-/

